1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
You've got a cast now,

2
00:00:02,624 --> 00:00:06,102
and so far nobody has said a word.

3
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:10,046
Today the harbormaster picks up the microphone.

4
00:00:10,946 --> 00:00:16,163
When the crew gets close to the hulk, she calls the ship,

5
00:00:16,613 --> 00:00:21,830
and what she says is different from one game to the next.

6
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:26,674
It's one scene and one short record,

7
00:00:27,124 --> 00:00:29,298
all in your fact sheet.

8
00:00:30,498 --> 00:00:36,150
First, the last of the lines that Lecture 11 marked for Class 2.

9
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,963
It reads every scene in a section called dialogue,

10
00:00:41,413 --> 00:00:44,022
so that's the section I write.

11
00:00:45,822 --> 00:00:49,300
A scene is a record, like everything else.

12
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:54,113
Speaker is who's talking, and it takes her key.

13
00:00:55,013 --> 00:01:00,665
When hail means this is a call that comes in to the ship.

14
00:01:01,565 --> 00:01:05,478
And the title is what the call is about,

15
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:08,972
which the crew reads before they answer.

16
00:01:09,872 --> 00:01:13,350
Below the fence come the lines she says,

17
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:17,278
and each one starts with a percent sign.

18
00:01:18,478 --> 00:01:21,087
I wrote three of those lines,

19
00:01:21,537 --> 00:01:24,146
but she won't say all three.

20
00:01:25,046 --> 00:01:27,220
Each one is a take,

21
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:31,583
which means one way of saying the same thing.

22
00:01:32,483 --> 00:01:36,396
Every time the scene plays, the game picks one.

23
00:01:38,196 --> 00:01:40,370
So write two or three,

24
00:01:40,820 --> 00:01:43,863
and she stops sounding like a recording.

25
00:01:44,763 --> 00:01:47,807
Just keep each take on one line,

26
00:01:48,257 --> 00:01:49,996
however long it gets.

27
00:01:51,196 --> 00:01:56,848
But what if she has two things to say, one after the other?

28
00:01:57,748 --> 00:01:59,487
Then I write blocks.

29
00:02:00,387 --> 00:02:04,735
A block starts with an at sign and her key,

30
00:02:05,185 --> 00:02:07,793
with nothing else on that line.

31
00:02:08,693 --> 00:02:10,433
So here's her greeting,

32
00:02:10,883 --> 00:02:12,622
and here's her question.

33
00:02:14,422 --> 00:02:17,900
The game takes one take from each block.

34
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,843
The crew reads the first, presses Continue,

35
00:02:22,293 --> 00:02:24,033
and reads the second.

36
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:30,885
Lint is clean, and yet if I played this now, nobody would call.

37
00:02:31,785 --> 00:02:35,263
A scene is only words on a page

38
00:02:35,713 --> 00:02:39,191
until something in the story places the call.

39
00:02:40,091 --> 00:02:45,309
And the thing that places it lives up here, among my quests.

40
00:02:46,509 --> 00:02:49,117
It's a record with three hashes,

41
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:53,046
so it stands by itself, outside the arc.

42
00:02:53,946 --> 00:02:58,293
The first line of the fence is the word Beat,

43
00:02:58,743 --> 00:03:03,091
alone, the way the word Arc was in Lecture 9.

44
00:03:03,991 --> 00:03:07,470
A beat is a moment in the story.

45
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:12,702
It isn't a job, and it's not in the Quest Log.

46
00:03:14,502 --> 00:03:17,111
Now, when does the moment come?

47
00:03:18,011 --> 00:03:20,185
Until today, after Starts when,

48
00:03:20,635 --> 00:03:23,243
you've written at once, or revealed.

49
00:03:24,143 --> 00:03:28,491
But that line takes the same words as Done when.

50
00:03:29,391 --> 00:03:32,435
So I write reach, derelict, five hundred,

51
00:03:32,885 --> 00:03:37,233
and those are the very words that finish Close Inspection.

52
00:03:39,033 --> 00:03:43,380
Then Action, which is what happens when the beat starts.

53
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:48,193
On the next line, two spaces and a dash,

54
00:03:48,643 --> 00:03:53,426
and then who calls, the word hails, and the scene's key.

55
00:03:54,626 --> 00:03:56,800
Lint knows this lecture well,

56
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:59,859
and the page has its tables.

57
00:04:00,759 --> 00:04:05,107
But two mistakes get past it, and you'll make both.

58
00:04:06,007 --> 00:04:10,789
If I leave out the Starts when line, lint says clean,

59
00:04:11,239 --> 00:04:15,152
and the call arrives the moment the game starts.

60
00:04:16,952 --> 00:04:23,474
And if I write her name after the at sign, in place of her key,

61
00:04:23,924 --> 00:04:25,663
lint says clean again.

62
00:04:26,563 --> 00:04:30,476
Now that line isn't the start of a block,

63
00:04:30,926 --> 00:04:33,535
so it becomes one more take,

64
00:04:33,985 --> 00:04:37,898
and every so often she says it out loud.

65
00:04:39,098 --> 00:04:41,707
Here's Comms before I've flown anywhere,

66
00:04:42,157 --> 00:04:43,896
and nobody is calling.

67
00:04:44,796 --> 00:04:47,839
So in we go, toward the hulk.

68
00:04:48,739 --> 00:04:50,478
Close Inspection is done,

69
00:04:50,928 --> 00:04:55,276
and there's the call, with her name and my title.

70
00:04:56,176 --> 00:04:59,220
I open it, and there she is,

71
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:02,278
with one of my three greetings.

72
00:05:03,178 --> 00:05:06,657
I press Continue, and she asks her question.

73
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:10,600
Then Close, and the call is over.

74
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,974
Two more things to see.

75
00:05:14,874 --> 00:05:18,787
This time I open the call and press Back,

76
00:05:19,237 --> 00:05:22,715
and it goes back in the list, unanswered.

77
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:26,224
So Comms can read a call

78
00:05:26,674 --> 00:05:30,587
and save it for when the captain is ready.

79
00:05:32,387 --> 00:05:35,430
And when I start the mission over,

80
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:38,054
the takes are picked again,

81
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:42,417
so she may greet me with a different line.

82
00:05:43,617 --> 00:05:47,530
Now it's your turn: give her a second call.

83
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:50,170
Write a second scene,

84
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:54,533
and a second beat that starts at the lifeboat.

85
00:05:56,333 --> 00:05:59,811
Next time, the crew gets to answer her.
